      "title": "Start with how long the need lasts",
      "narration": "Elena wants a dependable benefit for a lifelong family obligation. Traditional whole life combines permanent death protection with scheduled premiums and contractual cash values. The guarantees depend on meeting the policy's requirements. Compare the guaranteed schedule with any additional illustrated values, and check the sustainable cost. An early surrender may return much less than the premiums paid. The word permanent describes the intended coverage pattern; it does not excuse unpaid required premiums or erase loan obligations. A permanent need can make whole life relevant, but the amount and funding still need to fit the client's circumstances.",
